## Uncertain

- Resolved 2026-09-24 on the owner's screen: `shotguns.r870_mcs` is named REMINGTON 870 MCS in the game's HUD (it was listed as R870 MCS from Gamer Guides).
- `light_machine_guns.qbb_lsw` (QBB LSW): Spelling: no Activision page found names it. Gamer Guides and the Call of Duty Wiki write 'QBB LSW'; reprints of Treyarch's 2013 patch notes write 'QBB-LSW'. Check the hyphen on the owner's screen.
- `pistols.five_seven` (Five-seven): Capitalisation: no Activision page found names it. The Call of Duty Wiki writes 'Five-seven', Gamer Guides 'Five-Seven'. Black Ops II draws weapon names in mixed case (Activision's own Create-a-Class screenshots show 'Tac-45' and 'Mk 48'), so check the capital S on the owner's screen.
- `specials.combat_knife` (Combat Knife): Not a Create-a-Class pick: it is the knife a player holds when the class has no primary or secondary weapon (and after planting the Assault Shield). Its name and its place among the Specials (it counts toward the Specials' Diamond camo) come from community references only; Activision's own Create-a-Class screenshots only show a 'Personalize Knife' button. Check the name on the owner's screen.

## Community sites, used for what Activision no longer says

Nothing was taken from these that an Activision page gives; they supply the
names, classes and unlock levels no surviving Activision page states, and every
item that relies on them lists them in its `sources`. No picture came from them.

- [Call of Duty Wiki, "Call of Duty: Black Ops II"](https://callofduty.fandom.com/wiki/Call_of_Duty:_Black_Ops_II),
  its weapons list (read through the Wayback Machine's 2026-09-07 copy, as the
  live page refused the reader): every multiplayer weapon by class, the
  Peacekeeper marked as Revolution DLC.
- [Gamer Guides, Black Ops II primary weapons](https://www.gamerguides.com/call-of-duty-black-ops-ii/guide/multiplayer-guide/multiplayer-weapons/primary-weapons)
  and [secondary weapons](https://www.gamerguides.com/call-of-duty-black-ops-ii/guide/multiplayer-guide/multiplayer-weapons/secondary-weapons):
  each weapon's unlock level and in-game description, by class; the Assault
  Shield under "Special" among the primaries, the Crossbow and Ballistic Knife
  under "Special" among the secondaries.
- [Call of Duty Wiki, "Assault Shield"](https://callofduty.fandom.com/wiki/Assault_Shield)
  (2026-07-30 copy): "classified as a Special in the create-A-class section",
  unlocked at level 34.
- [Call of Duty Wiki, "Combat Knife"](https://callofduty.fandom.com/wiki/Combat_Knife)
  (2026-09-03 copy): when a player holds it, and that it counts toward the
  Specials' Diamond camo.
- [Steam Community guide, "The complete camoflauge guide"](https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=172521258):
  the Specials class is the Assault Shield, Crossbow, Ballistic Knife and
  Combat Knife.
- [IMFDb, "Call of Duty: Black Ops II"](https://www.imfdb.org/wiki/Call_of_Duty:_Black_Ops_II):
  cross-check only; it is organised by the real guns (the "S12" is its Saiga
  12K, the "DSR 50" its DSR-50), and the game names it gives agree with the
  list.

